Package: powermon
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: minimal laptop power monitor with a built-in time series store
 powermon records battery power, Intel RAPL energy (platform, package,
 cores, GPU), CPU load, temperature, fan speed, battery charge and backlight
 every few seconds into a compact append-only time series file, without
 file system I/O on the sampling path. It answers queries with statistics,
 terminal charts, SVG and CSV export.
 .
 The recorder runs as a systemd service: it opens the perf counters as root
 and then switches to the unprivileged "powermon" user.
